sec.p:
VTE (
Figure 2
): The occurrence of VTE after initiating anti-coagulant therapy was reported in 7 studies out of 9 included studies (Patients 2002, events 115; rivaroxaban 932, events 50; and enoxaparin 1070, 65 events). Analysis of data showed rivaroxaban group had a statistically insignificant reduced association with VTE occurrence (RR 0.83, 95% CI 0.58–1.18, I2 0%, P 0.3).

DVT (
Figure 3
): The occurrence of DVT after initiating anti-coagulant therapy was reported in 5 studies out of 9 included studies (Patients 637, events 23; rivaroxaban 319, events 10; and enoxaparin 318, 13 events). Data analysis showed rivaroxaban group had a statistically insignificant lower DVT occurrence (RR 0.77, 95% CI 0.28–2.09, I2 18%, P 0.6).

PE (
Figure 4
): Out of the 9 included studies, 5 studies reported recurrence of DVT after initiation of therapy (Patients 583, events 18; rivaroxaban 295, events 9; and enoxaparin 288, 9 events). Pooling of data showed rivaroxaban group had a statistically insignificant reduction in the incidence of PE recurrence (RR 0.95, 95% CI 0.36–2.47, I2 5%, P 0.91).

Mortality (
Figure 5
): 4 studies out of the selected 9 reported mortality in both groups (Patients 1534, events 377; rivaroxaban 703, events 140; and enoxaparin 831, events 237). Analysis showed that there was an insignificant reduction of mortality rivaroxaban as compared to enoxaparin (RR 0.74, 95% CI 0.46–1.20, I2 73%, P 0.23). Sensitivity analysis was done to identify the cause of high heterogeneity of our results. Alzghari et al 17 was identified as the outlier (removal of which lowered our I2% to 0%).

Major Bleeding (
Figure 6
): All studies reported incidents of major bleeding after using anti-coagulants (Patients 2276, events 99; rivaroxaban 1049, events 37; and enoxaparin 1227, events 62). Only Wysokinski et al 16 was ignored due to Houghton et al 15 being the more recent study to report the findings of the same population in the same research centre that Wysokinski et al used. Our analysis showed rivaroxaban caused a statically insignificant reduction in major bleeding (RR 0.79, 95% CI 0.53–1.18, I2 0%, P 0.25).
